wave 2: registry-driven llm-switch + generalized server.py + auth

T4: bin/llm-switch reads engines.json (UNIT/BOOT/CONTAINER/APINAME/HEALTHURL via registry.py eval).
  hermes profile, smoke model name, gpu-free threshold, mount check all registry-driven. Lifecycle
  (lock/busy/stop-all/wait-gpu/start/health/smoke/rollback/preempt/force) preserved. 3 tests against
  mock systemctl/nvidia-smi/curl (stop-other + start-target + hermes-write, unknown-target, status).

T5: server.py generalized: registry load at boot (fail loudly if malformed); endpoints /api/detect,
  /api/engines CRUD, /api/validate (three-step gate), /api/switch, /api/effort, /api/hermes-sync,
  /api/journal, /api/config. Bearer-token auth on mutating endpoints (403 without); read open. 4 tests.

Bug fixes found during build:
- importlib + Python 3.14 @dataclass needs sys.modules registration before exec_module.
- bash case cannot word-split a variable as a pattern list; use a membership check.
- ${UNIT[k]:-} is unbound under set -u for a missing assoc key; use ${UNIT[k]+set}.
- python http.server needs an explicit from-import, not __import__ (returns the parent package).
